"boojum" == The Vanishing Valor <boojum@u.washington.edu> writes:
> 	You know how they say that a little lump leavens the loaf?
> Let's apply that to nethack.  Put in yeast as a food.  Weight=1, but
> every 50 turns after you pick it up, it grows (by 1).  A cursed
> yeast would sustain the adventurer for 25 turns, an uncursed one for
> 50 turns, and a blessed one for 75 turns.  Whee

Interesting...
Of course, yeast needs water and organic food to sustain itself
and grow.  So it would need to consume potions of water, monster
corpses, and so on.  In the process of growing it would generate
heat and a lot of pungent gas.
To the adventurer with poor hygiene it could cause infections.

The yeast becomes dormant when cold, and can be killed by extreme
heat.  In either case it stops growing.

Heck, might as well make it start out as a monster (F), which
multiplies like gremlins in water, and eats nearby food items.


